  "2026-08-23T20:29:26.533Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: contract-derived census and shared SDK file-or-stdin primitive will cover every external-content --*-file surface, preserve real-path behavior, improve unreadable-path recovery, and prove piped heredoc use. Canonical pm-iktj is reused after all-status duplicate verification."
  "2026-08-23T21:57:50.433Z","harness:codex","Tracker repair evidence: removed only the newly added duplicate pm-m9xv implements row by its exact created_at signature; the canonical 2026-07-25 relationship remains intact."
  "2026-08-23T22:05:18.542Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-24: every external-content file flag in this scope accepts '-' as stdin through the shared SDK token resolver: update/close --body-file plus comments, notes, and learnings --file. Real paths retain prior behavior and unreadable/missing input produces structured recovery. CLI invocation contracts now declare argv/file/stdin modes and the docs include heredoc/pipeline examples. Focused linked tests, the disposable-tracker body-stdin check, 7,858-test exact 100% coverage, typecheck, security scan, and the complete lint/static stack pass. The duplicate relationship added during reconciliation was removed by exact signature; the canonical historical implements edge remains."
  "2026-08-23T22:39:08.695Z","harness:codex","Review finding: --body-file - creates an isolated stdin resolver after --description - or --stdin-json can consume the stream, causing unsettled-await exit/hang. Add an up-front command-wide single-consumer refusal and real-process regression proof."
  "2026-08-23T22:48:45.194Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: command-wide stdin ownership is validated before --stdin-json, --description -, --body-file -, or bulk --ids - can read. Competing consumers fail with usage exit 2 rather than an unsettled second read; real-process negative controls and registration/contract unit tests pass. All three linked-test groups pass in isolated schema trackers with local_source_ref trust and zero trust, assertion, or infrastructure failures. Final full proof passes 570 files / 7,858 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-15T19:27:03.514Z",maintainer-agent,"Dogfood confirmation 2026-07-15 (review pass #89): pm create --body-file - fails ENOENT body_file_unreadable (tries to open a file literally named \"-\"), forcing a scratch-file workaround mid-review. The error's own next_steps suggest \"ls -l \\\"-\\\"\" — the recovery bundle does not know stdin is the intent. This is exactly the convention gap this item owns; --body-file should be first on the flag list when implementing."
